{"name":"Trade Winds","hex":"#b7c5c6","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"trade winds","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of trade wind"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trade_winds"}],"entries":[{"title":"Trade winds","blocks":[{"text":"The trade winds, or easterlies, are east-to-west prevailing winds that flow in Earth's equatorial region. The trade winds blow mainly from the northeast in the Northern Hemisphere and from the southeast in the Southern Hemisphere, strengthening during the winter and when the Arctic oscillation is in its warm phase. Trade winds have been used by captains of sailing ships to cross the world's oceans for centuries. They enabled European colonization of the Americas, and trade routes to become established across the Atlantic Ocean and the Pacific Ocean."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Map_prevailing_winds_on_earth.png/330px-Map_prevailing_winds_on_earth.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trade_winds","wikidata":"Q160603"},{"title":"Trade Winds (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Trade Winds is a 1938 American comedy murder mystery film directed by Tay Garnett written by Dorothy Parker, Alan Campbell, and Frank R. Adams, based on the story by Tay Garnett. The film stars Fredric March and Joan Bennett. It was distributed by United Artists, and released on December 28, 1938."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/42/TRADE_WINDS_1938.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trade_Winds_(film)","wikidata":"Q3208680"},{"title":"Trade","blocks":[{"text":"Trade is the act by which people swap something of value to obtain another valuable item. It involves the transfer of goods and services from one person or entity (seller) to another (buyer), often in exchange for money."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Kaufmann-1568.png/330px-Kaufmann-1568.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trade","wikidata":"Q601401"},{"title":"Wind","blocks":[{"text":"Wind is the natural movement of air or other gases relative to a planet's surface. Winds occur on a range of scales, from thunderstorm flows lasting tens of minutes, to local breezes generated by heating of land surfaces and lasting a few hours, to global winds resulting from the difference in absorption of solar energy between the climate zones on Earth. The study of wind is known as anemology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif/330px-Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wind","wikidata":"Q8094"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Spanish_Galleon.jpg/250px-Spanish_Galleon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/08/Spanish_Galleon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Spanish_Galleon.jpg/250px-Spanish_Galleon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Spanish galleon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpanish_Galleon.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/MercadodeSanJuandeDios.jpg/500px-MercadodeSanJuandeDios.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/MercadodeSanJuandeDios.jpg/1280px-MercadodeSanJuandeDios.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipe